[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

; The world seen from the drivable boundary, looking outward.
;
; VISUAL PROOF ONLY — not a game scene. It exists so acceptance item 7's "grass
; still visible beyond" and the design document's "no wall or ground edge" can be
; captured before there is a kart to drive there.
;
; The viewpoint stands AT the boundary — x = +drivableExtent = 90 — at roughly the
; chase camera's eye height, looking outward along +X. That is the position the
; design document's scenario names ("the kart is held against the boundary at
; +/-drivableExtent"), and the evidence has to be taken from where the scenario
; says or it is evidence about something else.
;
; An earlier version of this file used an elevated oblique viewpoint 28 wu inside
; the limit, because it framed the grid and the horizon more informatively. Review
; caught that the spec scenario, the register entry and ambiguity A11 all describe
; a view FROM the boundary, and were resting on a capture from somewhere else.
; These numbers are a viewpoint, not a specification: nothing reads them but this
; capture.

[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://scenes/world.tscn" id="1_world"]

[node name="BoundaryView" type="Node3D"]

[node name="World" parent="." instance=ExtResource("1_world")]
